mains the author's.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:145:| A9 | A conformance table lists every applicable WCAG 2.2 AA success criterion, the test that covers it, and what the author must supply (a meaningful title or `labelledBy`, series names, units, the page's own structure). It also states the limits in section 3.8. | Published with each release; a CI check that every listed test exists | R11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:216:Automated checks establish structure: names, roles, focus order, contrast, text. They do not establish that a screen-reader user finds a chart understandable. The only evidence for that in 1.0 is A3's rehearsal by the developer on five reader and browser pairs, recorded as rehearsal. Axylo is built by one person with no access to study participants, so no claim of usability testing with disabled users is made, and the conformance table says so in those words. Reviewers proposed participant testing as a release gate; it is recorded here as a known limit instead.\nacceptance/matrix.json:2045:    \"statement\": \"A published WCAG 2.2 AA conformance table lists each applicable criterion, its test, author obligations and limits.\",\nacceptance/matrix.json:2060:          \"reason\": \"The acceptance checker validates named test references, but no published WCAG-by-success-criterion conformance table is present.\"\nacceptance/matrix.json:2067:          \"reason\": \"The acceptance checker validates named test references, but no published WCAG-by-success-criterion conformance table is present.\"\nacceptance/matrix.json:2074:          \"reason\": \"The acceptance checker validates named test references, but no published WCAG-by-success-criterion conformance table is present.\"\nacceptance/matrix.json:2081:          \"reason\": \"The acceptance checker validates named test references, but no published WCAG-by-success-criterion conformance table is present.\"\nacceptance/matrix.json:2088:          \"reason\": \"The acceptance checker validates named test referen